  "methodology_version": "0.7.3-draft",
  "question": "How do the largest health systems in the connectivity ledger reach their endpoints, and why did the system table show zero endpoints for them before FHI-73?",
  "answer": "The zero the system table showed before FHI-73 was not an absence. 6 of 6 systems publish a FHIR endpoint in Epic's brand file, and the NDH itself carries that endpoint for 5. For 5 of those 5, every copy has either no managingOrganization or one holding no practitioner roles in the state. In 6 of 6 no member organization carries partOf, and in 6 of 6 the system's own Epic brand lists none of its member organizations' NPIs. The systems hold 21,963 distinct clinicians. The system rollup now counts every tier the practitioner funnel counts, each labelled. Through a member organization or CMS enrollment, 21,460 of them reach an endpoint: 0 through the NDH or a vendor NPI on a URL listing 10 or fewer NPIs (the deterministic tiers), 839 through a vendor NPI on a practice-wide or brand-wide list, 18,268 through name or brand resolution (H53) and 2,353 through CMS enrollment (any enrolled group; the ledger counts enrollment only when it lands on the system's own endpoint).",
